---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Projects — Aravind Anilraj (phi5ic)"
  description="Systems engineering, distributed computing, and Linux kernel projects."
>
  <div class="space-y-10 font-mono">
    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="border border-[#2a0e2e] bg-[#100613] p-4 sm:p-5 rounded-sm space-y-1">
      <div class="text-[11px] text-[#854d80]">phi5ic@mesh ~ $ ls -la /projects/</div>
      <h1 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight flex items-center gap-2">
        <span>Projects &amp; Systems</span>
        <span class="text-[#ff2a85] text-xs font-normal">[source code]</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xs text-[#c9a6c5]">
        Distributed storage engines, kernel patches, and hardware stabilization systems.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="space-y-6">
      <!-- Nifsi -->
      <article class="border border-[#2a0e2e] bg-[#100613]/70 p-4 rounded-sm space-y-2">
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline justify-between gap-1">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <h2 class="text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-white">&gt; Nifsi</h2>
            <span class="text-xs text-[#ff2a85]">[Rust / Linux]</span>
          </div>
          <a href="https://github.com/phi5ic/Nifsi" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-xs text-[#ff79c6] hover:underline font-mono">
            [github.com/phi5ic/Nifsi &nearr;]
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-[#ecd2e8] leading-relaxed">
          An open-source distributed userspace operating system layer written in Rust for Linux clusters. Unifies heterogeneous physical machines into a shared FUSE filesystem, Raft-replicated metadata store, and ChaCha20-Poly1305 encrypted peer mesh. Features a novel <strong>HADR (Horizontal &amp; Diagonal Parity)</strong> erasure-coding storage engine with 4 KB slice-level homology repair and flat 3.0&times; write amplification.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 text-xs pt-2 border-t border-[#2a0e2e] text-[#ff2a85]">
          <a href="https://github.com/phi5ic/Nifsi" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="hover:text-[#ff79c6]">[github repo &nearr;]</a>
          <a href="/posts/what-i-learned-trying-to-beat-xor/" class="hover:text-[#ff79c6]">[storage deep dive &rarr;]</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/phi5ic/Nifsi/tree/main/benchmarks" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="hover:text-[#ff79c6]">[benchmarks &nearr;]</a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Linux Kernel Patches -->
      <article class="border border-[#2a0e2e] bg-[#100613]/70 p-4 rounded-sm space-y-2">
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline justify-between gap-1">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <h2 class="text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-white">&gt; Linux Kernel Upstream Patches</h2>
            <span class="text-xs text-[#00ff66]">[6 Merged]</span>
          </div>
          <a href="/patches/" class="text-xs text-[#ff79c6] hover:underline font-mono">
            [view patch table &rarr;]
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-[#ecd2e8] leading-relaxed">
          Patches submitted and merged into the upstream Linux kernel across the <strong>ASoC / Intel sound driver</strong> and <strong>Thermal / int340x</strong> subsystems. Resolved critical MCLK hardware clock resource leaks on Intel Baytrail/Cherrytrail boards and fixed shift overflow / sysfs error propagation bugs. Reviewed and signed off by maintainers Mark Brown and Rafael J. Wysocki.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 text-xs pt-2 border-t border-[#2a0e2e] text-[#ff2a85]">
          <a href="/patches/" class="hover:text-[#ff79c6]">[merged patch table &rarr;]</a>
          <a href="https://lore.kernel.org/all/?q=Aravind+Anilraj" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="hover:text-[#ff79c6]">[lore archive &nearr;]</a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- StabiSense -->
      <article class="border border-[#2a0e2e] bg-[#100613]/70 p-4 rounded-sm space-y-2">
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline justify-between gap-1">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <h2 class="text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-white">&gt; StabiSense</h2>
            <span class="text-xs text-[#bb9af7]">[IEEE Thailand 2026]</span>
          </div>
          <a href="https://github.com/phi5ic/StabiSense" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-xs text-[#ff79c6] hover:underline font-mono">
            [github.com/phi5ic/StabiSense &nearr;]
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-[#ecd2e8] leading-relaxed">
          Dynamic stabilization system designed for microchip sets during precision semiconductor manufacturing. Selected as a <strong>Myosa 5.0 Finalist</strong> and presented at the IEEE Thailand Biosensors Conference (2026).
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 text-xs pt-2 border-t border-[#2a0e2e] text-[#ff2a85]">
          <a href="https://github.com/phi5ic/StabiSense" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="hover:text-[#ff79c6]">[github repository &nearr;]</a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Qgis-Simulation -->
      <article class="border border-[#2a0e2e] bg-[#100613]/70 p-4 rounded-sm space-y-2">
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline justify-between gap-1">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <h2 class="text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-white">&gt; Qgis-Simulation</h2>
            <span class="text-xs text-[#00ff66]">[1st Place Hackathon]</span>
          </div>
          <a href="https://github.com/phi5ic/Qgis-Simulation" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-xs text-[#ff79c6] hover:underline font-mono">
            [github.com/phi5ic/Qgis-Simulation &nearr;]
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-[#ecd2e8] leading-relaxed">
          High-performance spatial analysis tool designed to detect water pipeline breaches by fusing machine learning terrain classification, Dijkstra's shortest-path flow algorithms, and Copernicus SAR satellite radar imagery. Awarded First Place at the Flowvision Hackathon (Brahma26, ASIET).
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 text-xs pt-2 border-t border-[#2a0e2e] text-[#ff2a85]">
          <a href="https://github.com/phi5ic/Qgis-Simulation" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="hover:text-[#ff79c6]">[github repository &nearr;]</a>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
